Helios DXVK fork: wait for other processes' hand-offs of shared images

Conduit guest/windows/docs/shared-surfaces.md section 4. Applied after 0006
by ci/windows/Build-Driver.ps1.

A keyed-mutex acquirer (or any reader after a cross-process flush) reads a
shared image through the Venus ring or NVK's RM channel, which dxgkrnl's
keyed mutex does not hold. The Helios UMD keeps a session-wide hand-off
ledger: at a hand-off the releaser publishes "device record d, point p" for
each shared resource (by KMD resource id), and its fence worker stores the
point's GPU completion. This patch is the reader's half:

- HeliosHandoffHooks (dxvk_helios_backend.h): sample/wait, installed by the
  UMD.
- DxvkImage::heliosHandoffKey / setHeliosHandoffKey: the resource id (an
  import has it from its sharing info, the UMD sets it on its own images).
- heliosPresentWaitBeforeRefresh samples the ledger for any shared image it
  reads (copy source, sampled view) and DxvkCommandList::waitHandoff records
  the point; the submission worker waits for it beside the producer waits,
  bounded. heliosNoteSampledShared now notes every shared image while the
  hooks are installed, so a creator reading what an opener wrote waits too.

